      "title": "National Universities",
      "caption_extra": "Education—Universities. Introduced as \"a list of the national and provincial universities, and also the important privately founded institutions recognized by the Ministry\"; the Provincial list follows on p. 317 (tables/p0342_1.json).",
      "continued": false,
      "parts": [
        {
          "label": null,
          "columns": [
            "Name",
            "Place",
            "Description"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Chekiang University",
              "Hangchow",
              "Has colleges of arts and sciences, agriculture, and engineering. There are about 400 students, and its annual expenditure is $869,000."
            ],
            [
              "Chinan University",
              "Chenju, near Shanghai",
              "Largely intended for overseas Chinese students. Has colleges of arts and sciences, law, education, and commerce. Its dissolution was decided upon by the Executive Yuan in 1932, but execution was postponed."
            ],
            [
              "Chiao Tung University",
              "Shanghai, Peiping, Tangshan",
              "The old Nanyang College, founded in 1896. In 1907 its control was transferred to the Ministry of Communications, and in 1928 to the Ministry of Railways. Has departments of electrical and mechanical engineering and railway administration."
            ],
            [
              "Chung Shan University",
              "Canton",
              "Formerly known as Kwangtung University. Renamed in honour of Dr. Sun Yat-sen. It is the central seat of learning in South China, and has colleges of arts and science, law, agriculture and forestry, and medicine. There are about 1,600 students and its annual expenditure is $1,775,000."
            ],
            [
              "National Central University",
              "Nanking",
              "Started July, 1927, in substitution for the former National South-Eastern University, Has colleges of arts, sciences, law, education, agriculture, and engineering. It is one of the biggest universities in China, with a budget of $1,720,000."
            ],
            [
              "National Peiyang Engineering College",
              "Tientsin",
              "Formerly Peiyang University. Since the transfer of its law school to Peiping, this institution has concentrated on engineering courses, comprising civil, mining, and metallurgical, mechanical and electrical. Has two research institutes on engineering materials and mining, and a research council on aeronautical engineering."
            ],
            [
              "Peiping Normal University",
              "Peiping",
              "Formerly Peking Teachers College. Has colleges of arts, sciences, and education."
            ],
            [
              "Peiping University",
              "Peiping",
              "Founded in 1927 as amalgamation of all colleges under Ministry of Education with exception of Peking University. Has colleges of arts, sciences, law, medicine and agriculture, with an annual budget of $1,437,108."
            ],
            [
              "Peking University",
              "Peiping",
              "This is the historic Imperial University, built in the Tsing Dynasty, and has been the centre of intellectual movements since 1918. Its annual budget is reduced to $900,000."
            ],
            [
              "Shantung University",
              "Tsingtao",
              "Has colleges of arts, sciences, and agriculture."
            ],
            [
              "Szechwan University",
              "Chengtu",
              "An amalgamation of all higher educational institutions of the province."
            ],
            [
              "Tsing Hua University",
              "Peiping",
              "This university is built upon the former Tsing Hua College, founded in 1911, as the result of the action of the United States Government in remitting to China G.$10,785,286 of the Boxer Indemnity. It was originally intended to be a preparatory school for training students to be sent to America to carry on advanced studies. A new policy of university development was adopted in 1925. Has colleges of arts, sciences, law and engineering. There is also a research institute."
            ],
            [
              "Tung Chi University",
              "Woosung, near Shanghai",
              "Conducted along the lines of a German technische hochschule with a few German instructors. Has colleges of engineering and medicine."
            ],
            [
              "Wu Han University",
              "Wuchang",
              "Composed of former Wuchang Normal College, Law College, and Commercial College. Has colleges of arts, sciences and law. There are about 300 students. Its annual expenditure is $857,000."
            ]
          ]
        }
